---
/**
 * Two short looping opening scenes of «Отражение и преломление света». No numbers and no signs in the pictures; the
 * captions' popovers explain.
 * Sunbeam: a room in a cut-away side view. Sunlight falls through the window at 30° to the horizontal (parallel
 *   rays). A hand holds a small mirror above the table and tilts it by +8° and −6°; the reflected beam is traced
 *   exactly (law of reflection from both ends of the mirror) to the right wall or the ceiling, so the bright spot
 *   («солнечный зайчик») runs along them: the beam turns twice as far as the mirror. The table, the mirror and the
 *   cat cast the correct parallel shadows of the sunlight; the cat's head follows the spot.
 * Coin: a cup in a cut-away side view, 10 px = 1 cm (inner width 10 cm, depth 7 cm). The eye looks over the rim: the
 *   line of sight grazing the rim meets the far wall above the bottom, so the coin is hidden. Water (n = 1,33) is
 *   poured to 6,2 cm. The ray from the coin's centre to the eye is found exactly with the law of refraction; from a
 *   level of about 4,4 cm it passes over the rim and the coin is seen. Its apparent place is where the backward
 *   extensions of two neighbouring rays reaching the eye meet: higher than the coin and nearer to the eye.
 * Plays only while visible; «Повторить» restarts.
 */
import IntroFrame from '@components/intro/IntroFrame.astro';
import More from '@components/More.astro';

const uid = Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 8);
const mSun = `li-sun-${uid}`;
const gSpot = `li-spot-${uid}`;
---

<IntroFrame data-lightintro>
	<div class="intro__card" data-scene="sunbeam">
		<svg class="intro__svg" viewBox="0 0 360 240" role="img" aria-label="Солнечный день, комната. Свет из окна падает на маленькое зеркальце в руке. Зеркальце чуть поворачивают — и солнечный зайчик быстро бежит по стене и потолку, а кошка следит за ним">
			<defs>
				<mask id={mSun} maskUnits="userSpaceOnUse" x="0" y="0" width="360" height="240">
					<rect x="0" y="0" width="360" height="240" fill="white"></rect>
					<!-- the shadow of the table top -->
					<polygon points="96,176 232,176 297.8,214 161.8,214" fill="black"></polygon>
				</mask>
				<radialGradient id={gSpot}>
					<stop offset="0" stop-color="var(--ig-v)" stop-opacity="0.9"></stop>
					<stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--ig-v)" stop-opacity="0"></stop>
				</radialGradient>
			</defs>
			<rect class="li-wall" x="0" y="0" width="360" height="240"></rect>
			<rect class="li-ceil" x="0" y="0" width="360" height="12"></rect>
			<rect class="li-side" x="344" y="12" width="16" height="202"></rect>
			<rect class="li-floor" x="0" y="214" width="360" height="26"></rect>
			<!-- the window in the left wall -->
			<rect class="li-side" x="0" y="12" width="16" height="202"></rect>
			<rect class="li-glass" x="2" y="26" width="12" height="78"></rect>
			<line class="li-frame" x1="8" y1="26" x2="8" y2="104"></line>
			<!-- sunlight: a faint band through the air and bright patches where it falls -->
			<g mask={`url(#${mSun})`}>
				<polygon class="li-band" points="16,26 16,104 206.5,214 341.6,214"></polygon>
			</g>
			<line class="li-patch" x1="140.7" y1="176" x2="232" y2="176"></line>
			<line class="li-patch" x1="297.8" y1="214" x2="341.6" y2="214"></line>
			<line class="li-shade" x1="0" y1="176" x2="0" y2="176" data-mshade></line>
			<!-- the table -->
			<rect class="li-table" x="96" y="176" width="136" height="6" rx="1.5"></rect>
			<rect class="li-table" x="102" y="182" width="6" height="32"></rect>
			<rect class="li-table" x="220" y="182" width="6" height="32"></rect>
			<!-- the cat on the floor, in the sun -->
			<path class="li-cat" d="M 322 214 C 336 214 334 196 322 190 C 312 186 300 192 298 204 C 297 211 304 214 312 214 Z"></path>
			<path class="li-tail" d="M 330 211 C 346 208 348 196 340 190" data-tail></path>
			<g data-cathead>
				<circle class="li-cat" cx="0" cy="0" r="9.5"></circle>
				<path class="li-cat" d="M -8 -4 L -7 -15 L -1 -8 Z M 8 -4 L 7 -15 L 1 -8 Z"></path>
				<circle class="li-cateye" cx="-3.5" cy="-1" r="1.6" data-ceye></circle>
				<circle class="li-cateye" cx="3.5" cy="-1" r="1.6" data-ceye></circle>
			</g>
			<!-- the reflected beam and the sunbeam spot -->
			<polygon class="li-beam" points="" data-beam></polygon>
			<ellipse fill={`url(#${gSpot})`} rx="16" ry="16" data-glow></ellipse>
			<polyline class="li-spot" points="" data-spot></polyline>
			<!-- the arm and the hand with the mirror (turned about the mirror's centre) -->
			<path class="li-sleeve" d="" data-arm></path>
			<g data-mirror>
				<rect class="li-handle" x="-2.5" y="2" width="5" height="18" rx="2"></rect>
				<rect class="li-skin" x="-7" y="12" width="14" height="13" rx="5"></rect>
				<line class="li-mback" x1="-13" y1="1.6" x2="13" y2="1.6"></line>
				<line class="li-mface" x1="-13" y1="0" x2="13" y2="0"></line>
			</g>
		</svg>
		<div class="intro__foot">
			<p>Стоит чуть повернуть зеркальце, и солнечный зайчик убегает далеко по стене: <More term="свет от зеркальца поворачивается вдвое сильнее, чем само зеркальце">Зеркальце повернули на 8° — отражённый свет повернулся на 16°. Так получается потому, что угол отражения всегда равен углу падения. Подробно — в разделе <a href="#закон-отражения-света">«Закон отражения света»</a>.</More>.</p>
			<button type="button" class="intro__again" data-again>Повторить</button>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="intro__card" data-scene="coin">
		<svg class="intro__svg" viewBox="0 0 360 240" role="img" aria-label="Человек смотрит в чашку, монету на дне заслоняет край чашки. В чашку наливают воду — и монета становится видна, хотя её никто не трогал">
			<rect class="li-wall" x="0" y="0" width="360" height="240"></rect>
			<rect class="li-tabletop" x="0" y="202" width="360" height="38"></rect>
			<line class="li-edge" x1="0" y1="202" x2="360" y2="202"></line>
			<!-- the person: head in profile looking right and down -->
			<path class="li-shirt" d="M 14 240 C 16 150 46 112 64 112 C 90 112 104 160 106 240 Z"></path>
			<circle class="li-skin" cx="58" cy="80" r="22"></circle>
			<path class="li-hair" d="M 36 80 C 34 58 52 50 66 56 C 74 59 78 64 79 70 C 70 64 58 64 50 70 C 44 74 42 80 36 80 Z"></path>
			<path class="li-skin" d="M 79 78 L 85 86 L 79 88 Z"></path>
			<path class="li-eye" d="M 72 74 Q 76.5 70.5 80.5 74 Q 76.5 77 72 74 Z"></path>
			<circle class="li-pupil" cx="78" cy="74" r="1.7"></circle>
			<!-- the cup: inner 170–270, rim at 126, bottom at 196 -->
			<path class="li-water" d="" data-water></path>
			<line class="li-surface" x1="170" y1="196" x2="270" y2="196" data-surface></line>
			<g data-coin>
				<rect class="li-coin" x="242" y="193" width="20" height="3" rx="1"></rect>
			</g>
			<path class="li-cup" d="M 164 126 H 170 V 196 H 270 V 126 H 276 V 202 H 164 Z"></path>
			<!-- the line of sight grazing the rim (dry cup) -->
			<path class="li-sight" d="" data-sight></path>
			<!-- the ray from the coin to the eye, its extension and the coin as the eye sees it -->
			<path class="li-ext" d="" data-ext></path>
			<g data-ghost>
				<rect class="li-ghost" x="-10" y="-1.5" width="20" height="3" rx="1"></rect>
			</g>
			<g class="li-ray" data-ray>
				<path class="li-ray__glow" d=""></path>
				<path class="li-ray__core" d=""></path>
				<path class="li-ray__flow" d=""></path>
			</g>
			<!-- the jug, turned about its spout -->
			<path class="li-stream" d="" data-stream></path>
			<g data-jug>
				<path class="li-jug" d="M 0 0 L 10 -6 L 46 -6 Q 52 -6 52 2 L 50 44 Q 49 52 40 52 L 16 52 Q 8 52 7 44 L 5 10 Z"></path>
				<path class="li-jugh" d="M 51 6 C 66 6 68 32 50 36"></path>
			</g>
		</svg>
		<div class="intro__foot">
			<p>Монету на дне чашки заслоняет край. Нальём воды, и монета покажется, <More term="хотя её никто не сдвигал">Лучи от монеты, выходя из воды в воздух, меняют направление и проходят над краем чашки прямо в глаз. Глаз видит монету там, откуда луч как будто пришёл по прямой, — выше, чем она лежит. Это преломление света, подробно — в разделе <a href="#ложка-в-стакане-и-кажущаяся-глубина">«Ложка в стакане и кажущаяся глубина»</a>.</More>.</p>
			<button type="button" class="intro__again" data-again>Повторить</button>
		</div>
	</div>
</IntroFrame>

<style is:global>
	[data-lightintro] {
		--li-wall: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 8%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
		--li-skin: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ig-v) 30%, var(--sl-color-gray-4));
		--li-wood: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 30%, var(--sl-color-gray-4));
		--li-cat: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ig-v) 40%, var(--sl-color-gray-3));
	}
	:root[data-theme='light'] [data-lightintro] {
		--li-wall: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 6%, var(--sl-color-gray-6));
		--li-skin: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ig-v) 30%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
		--li-wood: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 35%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
		--li-cat: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ig-v) 55%, var(--sl-color-gray-4));
	}
	.li-wall {
		fill: var(--li-wall);
	}
	.li-ceil,
	.li-side {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-gray-4) 70%, var(--li-wall));
	}
	.li-floor {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 18%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
	}
	.li-glass {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-vx) 30%, transparent);
	}
	.li-frame {
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 2;
	}
	.li-band {
		fill: var(--ig-v);
		opacity: 0.13;
	}
	.li-patch {
		stroke: var(--ig-v);
		stroke-width: 3;
		opacity: 0.8;
	}
	.li-shade {
		stroke: var(--li-wood);
		stroke-width: 3.2;
	}
	.li-table {
		fill: var(--li-wood);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 0.8;
	}
	.li-cat {
		fill: var(--li-cat);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 0.8;
		stroke-linejoin: round;
	}
	.li-tail {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--li-cat);
		stroke-width: 4;
		stroke-linecap: round;
	}
	.li-cateye {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}
	.li-beam {
		fill: var(--ig-v);
		opacity: 0.22;
	}
	.li-spot {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--ig-v);
		stroke-width: 5;
		stroke-linecap: round;
		stroke-linejoin: round;
	}
	.li-sleeve {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-vx) 35%, var(--sl-color-gray-4));
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}
	.li-skin {
		fill: var(--li-skin);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}
	.li-handle {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.li-mback {
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 2.4;
		stroke-linecap: round;
	}
	.li-mface {
		stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-gray-1) 80%, var(--ig-vx));
		stroke-width: 2.4;
		stroke-linecap: round;
	}
	/* the coin scene */
	.li-tabletop {
		fill: var(--li-wood);
	}
	.li-edge {
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}
	.li-shirt {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-vy) 35%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}
	.li-hair {
		fill: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ig-vy) 25%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
	}
	.li-eye {
		fill: var(--sl-color-white);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 0.8;
	}
	:root[data-theme='light'] .li-eye {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-7, #fff);
	}
	.li-pupil {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}
	:root[data-theme='light'] .li-pupil {
		fill: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
	}
	.li-cup {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-gray-2) 60%, var(--sl-color-gray-5));
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		stroke-width: 1;
	}
	.li-water {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-vx) 28%, transparent);
	}
	.li-surface {
		stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-vx) 75%, var(--sl-color-white));
		stroke-width: 1.5;
	}
	.li-coin {
		fill: var(--ig-v);
		stroke: color-mix(in oklab, var(--ig-v) 60%, var(--sl-color-gray-2));
		stroke-width: 0.8;
	}
	.li-ghost {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 35%, transparent);
		stroke: var(--ig-v);
		stroke-width: 1;
		stroke-dasharray: 2.5 2;
	}
	.li-sight {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		stroke-width: 1.3;
		stroke-dasharray: 5 4;
	}
	.li-ext {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--ig-v);
		stroke-width: 1.3;
		stroke-dasharray: 4 4;
	}
	.li-ray {
		fill: none;
		stroke-linecap: round;
		stroke-linejoin: round;
	}
	.li-ray__glow {
		stroke: var(--ig-v);
		stroke-width: 6;
		opacity: 0.2;
	}
	.li-ray__core {
		stroke: var(--ig-v);
		stroke-width: 1.8;
	}
	.li-ray__flow {
		stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-v) 30%, white);
		stroke-width: 3;
		stroke-dasharray: 2 18;
		animation: li-flow 0.8s linear infinite;
	}
	@keyframes li-flow {
		to {
			stroke-dashoffset: -20;
		}
	}
	.li-jug {
		fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--sl-color-gray-2) 25%, transparent);
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		stroke-width: 1.5;
		stroke-linejoin: round;
	}
	.li-jugh {
		fill: none;
		stroke: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		stroke-width: 3;
		stroke-linecap: round;
	}
	.li-stream {
		fill: none;
		stroke: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ig-vx) 60%, transparent);
		stroke-width: 3.5;
		stroke-linecap: round;
	}
</style>

<script>
	import { scene, clamp } from '@components/intro/scene';

	type P = { x: number; y: number };
	const smooth = (a: number, b: number, x: number) => {
		const t = clamp((x - a) / (b - a));
		return t * t * (3 - 2 * t);
	};
	const f1 = (v: number) => v.toFixed(1);
	const f2 = (v: number) => v.toFixed(2);
	const RAD = Math.PI / 180;
	const pts = (ps: P[]) => ps.map((p) => `${f1(p.x)},${f1(p.y)}`).join(' ');

	for (const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-lightintro]')) {
		// Sunbeam: the mirror turns to +8°, holds, turns to −6°, back to 0; 8 s
		{
			const card = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene="sunbeam"]')!;
			const $ = <T extends Element>(s: string) => card.querySelector<T>(s)!;
			const mirror = $<SVGGElement>('[data-mirror]');
			const arm = $<SVGPathElement>('[data-arm]');
			const beam = $<SVGPolygonElement>('[data-beam]');
			const spot = $<SVGPolylineElement>('[data-spot]');
			const glow = $<SVGEllipseElement>('[data-glow]');
			const shade = $<SVGLineElement>('[data-mshade]');
			const head = $<SVGGElement>('[data-cathead]');
			const tail = $<SVGPathElement>('[data-tail]');
			const M = { x: 150, y: 142 };
			const HALF = 13;
			const D = { x: Math.cos(30 * RAD), y: Math.sin(30 * RAD) }; // sunlight, 30° below the horizontal
			const WALL = 344;
			const CEIL = 12;
			const HEAD = { x: 300, y: 188 };
			/** where a ray from p along d meets the right wall or the ceiling */
			const hit = (p: P, d: P): P => {
				const tw = (WALL - p.x) / d.x;
				const tc = d.y < 0 ? (CEIL - p.y) / d.y : Infinity;
				const t = Math.min(tw, tc);
				return { x: p.x + d.x * t, y: p.y + d.y * t };
			};
			scene(card, 8, (x) => {
				const s = x * 8;
				// the tilt of the mirror, degrees (positive: counterclockwise on screen, the beam goes higher)
				const phi = 8 * smooth(0.08, 0.3, x) - 14 * smooth(0.45, 0.7, x) + 6 * smooth(0.8, 0.95, x);
				const a = -phi * RAD; // screen angle of the mirror line
				const u = { x: Math.cos(a), y: Math.sin(a) };
				const n = { x: u.y, y: -u.x }; // normal pointing up (the reflecting face)
				const dn = D.x * n.x + D.y * n.y;
				const r = { x: D.x - 2 * dn * n.x, y: D.y - 2 * dn * n.y };
				const p1 = { x: M.x - HALF * u.x, y: M.y - HALF * u.y };
				const p2 = { x: M.x + HALF * u.x, y: M.y + HALF * u.y };
				const h1 = hit(p1, r);
				const h2 = hit(p2, r);
				const corner = Math.abs(h1.x - h2.x) > 0.01 && Math.abs(h1.y - h2.y) > 0.01 ? [{ x: WALL, y: CEIL }] : [];
				const ends = [h1, ...corner, h2];
				beam.setAttribute('points', pts([p1, ...ends, p2]));
				spot.setAttribute('points', pts(ends));
				const c = { x: (h1.x + h2.x) / 2, y: (h1.y + h2.y) / 2 };
				glow.setAttribute('cx', f1(c.x));
				glow.setAttribute('cy', f1(c.y));
				// the mirror's shadow on the table top (parallel sunlight down to y = 176)
				const sh = (p: P) => p.x + ((176 - p.y) / D.y) * D.x; // M.y = 142: the shadow falls on the table top
				shade.setAttribute('x1', f1(Math.min(sh(p1), sh(p2))));
				shade.setAttribute('x2', f1(Math.max(sh(p1), sh(p2))));
				mirror.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${M.x} ${M.y}) rotate(${f2(-phi)})`);
				// the forearm from below the picture to the fist under the mirror, 14 px wide
				const fist = { x: M.x - 18.5 * Math.sin(a), y: M.y + 18.5 * Math.cos(a) };
				const A = { x: 96, y: 250 };
				const len = Math.hypot(fist.x - A.x, fist.y - A.y);
				const nx = (-(fist.y - A.y) / len) * 7;
				const ny = ((fist.x - A.x) / len) * 7;
				arm.setAttribute(
					'd',
					`M ${f1(A.x + nx)} ${f1(A.y + ny)} L ${f1(fist.x + nx)} ${f1(fist.y + ny)} L ${f1(fist.x - nx)} ${f1(fist.y - ny)} L ${f1(A.x - nx)} ${f1(A.y - ny)} Z`,
				);
				// the cat looks at the spot
				const look = (Math.atan2(c.y - HEAD.y, c.x - HEAD.x) * 180) / Math.PI;
				const tilt = Math.max(-25, Math.min(25, (look + 90) * 0.5));
				head.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${HEAD.x} ${HEAD.y}) rotate(${f1(tilt)})`);
				tail.setAttribute('transform', `rotate(${f1(6 * Math.sin(s * 2.2))} 330 211)`);
			});
		}

		// Coin: the jug tilts (0,08 → 0,16), water is poured up to 6,2 cm (0,16 → 0,72), the jug goes back; 9 s
		{
			const card = root.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-scene="coin"]')!;
			const $ = <T extends Element>(s: string) => card.querySelector<T>(s)!;
			const water = $<SVGPathElement>('[data-water]');
			const surface = $<SVGLineElement>('[data-surface]');
			const sight = $<SVGPathElement>('[data-sight]');
			const ext = $<SVGPathElement>('[data-ext]');
			const ghost = $<SVGGElement>('[data-ghost]');
			const ray = [...card.querySelectorAll<SVGPathElement>('[data-ray] path')];
			const rayG = $<SVGGElement>('[data-ray]');
			const jug = $<SVGGElement>('[data-jug]');
			const stream = $<SVGPathElement>('[data-stream]');
			const N = 1.33;
			const E = { x: 78, y: 74 }; // the eye
			const RIM = { x: 170, y: 126 }; // the inner top corner of the near wall
			const Q = { x: 252, y: 193 }; // the coin's centre
			const BOTTOM = 196;
			const FULL = 62; // px of water = 6,2 cm
			/** the point on the surface y = ys where the refracted ray from q reaches the eye e */
			const exitAt = (q: P, e: P, ys: number) => {
				let lo = e.x;
				let hi = q.x;
				for (let k = 0; k < 50; k++) {
					const xs = (lo + hi) / 2;
					const sa = (xs - e.x) / Math.hypot(xs - e.x, ys - e.y);
					const sg = (q.x - xs) / Math.hypot(q.x - xs, q.y - ys);
					if (sa > N * sg) hi = xs;
					else lo = xs;
				}
				return { x: (lo + hi) / 2, y: ys };
			};
			const meet = (p1: P, d1: P, p2: P, d2: P): P => {
				const den = d1.x * d2.y - d1.y * d2.x;
				const t = ((p2.x - p1.x) * d2.y - (p2.y - p1.y) * d2.x) / den;
				return { x: p1.x + d1.x * t, y: p1.y + d1.y * t };
			};
			// the dry line of sight: from the eye over the rim to the far wall
			const k0 = (RIM.y - E.y) / (RIM.x - E.x);
			sight.setAttribute('d', `M ${E.x} ${E.y} L 270 ${f1(RIM.y + k0 * (270 - RIM.x))}`);
			scene(card, 9, (x) => {
				const fill = smooth(0.16, 0.72, x);
				const h = FULL * fill;
				const ys = BOTTOM - h;
				water.setAttribute('d', `M 170 ${f1(ys)} H 270 V ${BOTTOM} H 170 Z`);
				surface.setAttribute('y1', f1(ys));
				surface.setAttribute('y2', f1(ys));
				surface.style.opacity = h > 0.5 ? '1' : '0';
				sight.style.opacity = f2(0.9 * (1 - smooth(0.2, 0.3, x)));
				// the jug: tilts to pour, comes back; its water runs out
				const tilt = smooth(0.08, 0.16, x) * (1 - smooth(0.72, 0.8, x));
				jug.setAttribute('transform', `translate(244 46) rotate(${f1(-62 * tilt)})`);
				const pour = x > 0.15 && x < 0.73 ? 1 : 0;
				stream.setAttribute('d', pour ? `M 244 47 C 241 70 238 ${f1(ys - 30)} 238 ${f1(ys)}` : '');
				// the ray from the coin to the eye, when it passes over the rim
				let vis = 0;
				if (h > 4) {
					const S = exitAt(Q, E, ys);
					const yRim = S.y + ((E.y - S.y) * (RIM.x - S.x)) / (E.x - S.x);
					vis = S.x >= RIM.x && yRim < RIM.y ? clamp((RIM.y - yRim) / 3) : 0;
					if (vis > 0) {
						const d = `M ${f1(Q.x)} ${f1(Q.y)} L ${f1(S.x)} ${f1(S.y)} L ${E.x} ${E.y}`;
						ray.forEach((p) => p.setAttribute('d', d));
						// the apparent place: backward extensions of the rays to two neighbouring points of the pupil
						const E2 = { x: E.x, y: E.y - 3 };
						const S2 = exitAt(Q, E2, ys);
						const A = meet(S, { x: S.x - E.x, y: S.y - E.y }, S2, { x: S2.x - E2.x, y: S2.y - E2.y });
						ext.setAttribute('d', `M ${f1(S.x)} ${f1(S.y)} L ${f1(A.x)} ${f1(A.y)}`);
						ghost.setAttribute('transform', `translate(${f1(A.x)} ${f1(A.y)})`);
					}
				}
				rayG.style.opacity = f2(vis);
				ext.style.opacity = f2(vis);
				ghost.style.opacity = f2(vis);
			});
		}
	}
</script>
